      "message": "This unaligned error case is impossible, right? The `ResMemEntry` can be `derive(zerocopy::Unaligned)`. With that, you can write this and be assured that unaligned errors are statically impossible:\n\n```\n// outside\nuse zerocopy::{SizeError, Unaligned};\n\n\n#[repr(C)]\n#[derive(\n    Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, Eq, FromBytes, Immutable, IntoBytes, KnownLayout, PartialEq, Unaligned\n)]\npub(crate) struct ResMemEntry {\n    vm_name_offset: U32\u003cNativeEndian\u003e,\n    blob_offset: U32\u003cNativeEndian\u003e,\n    blob_size: U32\u003cNativeEndian\u003e,\n    compat_offset: U32\u003cNativeEndian\u003e,\n    flags: U32\u003cNativeEndian\u003e,\n}\n\nimpl\u003cSrc, Dst: ?Sized\u003e From\u003cSizeError\u003cSrc, Dst\u003e\u003e for Error {\n    fn from(x: SizeError\u003cSrc, Dst\u003e) -\u003e Error { Error::InconsistentSize }\n}\n\n// here\nlet (entries, buffer) \u003d \u003c[ResMemEntry]\u003e::ref_from_prefix_with_elems(rem, count as usize)\n    .map_err(SizeError::from)?;\n```",
